{"entity": "GPT-4o-mini", "type": "method", "description": "GPT-4o-mini is a powerful multimodal language model with native text and image understanding capabilities and a 128K token context window. It serves as a backbone LLM and baseline in experimental frameworks, and is used to conduct all accuracy evaluations throughout these frameworks, ensuring consistent, reliable, and consistent assessment standards.\n\nAs a method, GPT-4o-mini was evaluated on the DocBench dataset, achieving an overall accuracy of 51.2%, and on MMLongBench, achieving an overall accuracy of 33.5%. As a baseline model, it demonstrated several incorrect responses across various tasks: it incorrectly identified VAE as having clearer separation in a multi-panel figure interpretation case; it incorrectly answered DKK 32,928 million for Novo Nordisk's wages and salaries in 2020; it provided an incorrect answer regarding the lowest accuracy GCAN configuration for Twitter15; and it incorrectly identified the BERT-to-BERT model with an AUPRC of 0.455 as the highest performer for the Evidence Inference dataset. Additionally, GPT-4o-mini was evaluated in a multimodal RAG failure case, producing an incorrect answer about the NER label generation sequence, and in a cross-modal noise case, providing an incorrect answer regarding joint goal accuracy improvements in the Train domain."}
